    "intro": "Asparagus is one of the finest spring vegetables: a long-lived perennial which gives a fresh, delicate crop just when the garden is short of new green shoots. It is not difficult once established, but it asks for space, clean ground and patience. Treat the bed as a permanent feature: clear perennial weeds thoroughly, improve the soil before planting and do not crop hard while the crowns are young. In return, a good bed can produce spears for many years, followed by tall ferny summer growth which feeds the roots for the next season.",
